course: dictionary
lesson: 9175
title: Snuggle and warm feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word like snuggle often tells you how something feels, not just what someone does. Look at the words around it first. «In cartoons winter animals snuggle in cosy burrows with scarves on.» Animals in winter need to be warm, and scarves and cosy burrows show that. So snuggle must mean getting into a warm, comfortable place.
explain: Snuggle can also mean holding someone close and cuddling them. Ask yourself: who is snuggling, and where? A child snuggling with a parent or a pet is showing love and safety. The same word can mean getting comfortable or giving a cuddle, so the context decides which meaning fits.
explain: Look for the little words that go with snuggle: «snuggle up», «snuggle down» and «snuggle into». Up, down and into all show movement towards a warm, cosy place. When you meet a new phrase, try swapping in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Snuggle means to get into a warm, comfortable position, often close to someone or under a blanket.
fact: Snuggle can also mean to hold someone close and cuddle them.
fact: As a noun, a snuggle is a cuddle.
fact: Snuggle up, snuggle down and snuggle into are common phrases that show getting cosy.
fact: In stories, snuggling shows warmth, safety and love.
exercise: «In cartoons winter animals snuggle in cosy burrows with scarves on.» What does snuggle mean here? | To shout loudly | To run very fast | To swim under water | *To get into a warm, comfortable position
exercise: Mum says, «Let's snuggle down with a book.» What does snuggle down mean? | *Get comfortable and settle in warmly | Leave the room quickly | Wash the dishes | Jump up and dance
exercise: Dad gives Ella a big snuggle. What is a snuggle? | A loud noise | A type of hat | A race | *A cuddle
test: Ben wants to snuggle his dog on the sofa. What does snuggle suggest about how Ben feels? | Hungry and in a hurry | Cold and lost | Angry and bored | *Warm, safe and loving
test: Which form of snuggle is a noun? | snuggling | *a snuggle | snuggled | snuggles the dog
exam: What does snuggle mean in «The kitten will snuggle into the blanket»? | To tear the blanket apart | To shout for help | To jump over the blanket | *To get into a warm, comfortable position
